  "instructions": [
    "Combine the water, almond milk, oats, cinnamon, and salt in a medium saucepan. Bring the mixture to a rolling boil over medium-high heat.",
    "Reduce the heat to low to maintain a gentle simmer. Cook the oats for 5 to 7 minutes, checking at 5 minutes, until the liquid is absorbed and the oats are tender.",
    "Pour the liquid egg whites into the simmering oats in a slow stream while stirring vigorously to prevent scrambling.",
    "Cook and stir the mixture for 2 to 3 minutes, checking at 2 minutes, until it becomes thick and the egg whites are opaque.",
    "Remove the saucepan from the heat. Stir in the frozen berries and vanilla extract so the residual heat thaws the fruit.",
    "Divide the warm oatmeal between two bowls. Top with the chopped walnuts before serving."
  ],
